\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Flipping the field on a finite graph}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{In the finite quartic model of \ref{fdip-00GJ}, replacing every real
field value by its negative preserves both the incidence energy and
the fourth powers. By \ref{fdip-00GL} the flip therefore preserves its probability law. A field restricted to two
values, #{+1} and #{-1}, can also be flipped at every vertex. What
edge and site weights respect this flip? What if each value can
instead be rotated through three positions?}
